---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const updated = '28 July 2026';

/**
 * This page exists to be checkable. The claim "we set no cookies" is worth nothing if a
 * reader cannot verify it in ten seconds, so the page tells them exactly how — and the
 * Playwright suite asserts the same thing on every route so it cannot quietly stop being true.
 */
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Cookies"
  description="This website sets no cookies. Here is how to check that for yourself in ten seconds."
>
  <section class="bg-navy text-white py-16 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <span class="eyebrow text-accent-onDark tick-on-dark">Cookies</span>
      <h1 class="mt-2 text-display-sm md:text-display-md leading-tight">
        This website sets no cookies.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-5 text-lg text-white/90 leading-relaxed">
        Not analytics cookies, not advertising cookies, not "strictly necessary" cookies. There
        is no banner because there is nothing to consent to, and no preference centre because
        there is no preference to express.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-5 text-muted-onDark">Last updated {updated}.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-10 text-white/80 leading-relaxed">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Check it yourself</h2>
        <p>
          Open your browser's developer tools on any page of this site, go to the console, and
          type:
        </p>
        <pre
          class="mt-4 bg-navy text-white/90 rounded-lg p-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code>document.cookie</code></pre>
        <p class="mt-4">
          You should get an empty string. Our automated tests assert exactly that on every route,
          so if it ever stops being true, the build breaks before you see it. If you find a
          cookie here, that is a defect and we would like to hear about it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Then how do you count visitors?</h2>
        <p>
          Plausible Analytics, which is EU-owned, EU-hosted and cookieless. It counts page views
          without setting a cookie and without building a persistent identifier for you. It
          processes your IP address in order to derive a country and to de-duplicate a visit
          within a day, and does not store the address itself. There is no cross-site tracking,
          no advertising network and no data sale. The
          <a href="/privacy" class="text-accent-onDark font-semibold hover:text-white">privacy page</a>
          has the detail, including the lawful basis.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Why we bothered</h2>
        <p>
          Under the ePrivacy Directive as implemented in Ireland, consent is required for storing
          or accessing information on your device unless it is strictly necessary for a service
          you asked for. The usual response is a banner. We took the other option: remove the
          things that need consent. That meant self-hosting fonts rather than loading them from a
          third-party CDN, choosing cookieless analytics, and not embedding third-party forms,
          video players or chat widgets.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          It is also a straightforward matter of respect. The first thing a website can do to a
          visitor is ask them to negotiate before reading. We would rather not.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">What about the product?</h2>
        <p>
          The MESvantage application is a different matter and is not covered by this page. Like
          any system with authenticated users, it uses a session cookie to keep you signed in —
          which is strictly necessary for a service you explicitly requested, and therefore not
          something you are asked to consent to. It sets no analytics or advertising cookies of
          any kind. Data processing inside a customer environment is governed by the signed
          agreement and its data processing addendum, not by this website's policies.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="border-t border-rule-onDark pt-8">
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-onDark">
          Questions to
          <a href="mailto:hello@mesvantage.com" class="text-accent-onDark font-semibold hover:text-white"
            >hello@mesvantage.com</a
          >.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
